@startuml
!theme plain
title For Product Owners:\nWhy Your App Needs Access Review Integration

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam activity {
    FontSize 12
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFFFCC
    BorderColor #CCCC00
    FontSize 11
}

start
:Your application has users\nwith different access levels;

partition "WITHOUT Integration" #FFEEEE {
    :No one reviews who\nhas access to your app;

    fork
        #CC3333:SOX / SOC2 AUDIT FINDING\n"Unreviewed application access"\nMaterial weakness\nCost: $1.8M+ to remediate;
    fork again
        #CC3333:TERMINATED EMPLOYEE\nretains access 116 days avg\nOrphan accounts undetected\nInsider threat: $16.2M avg;
    fork again
        #CC3333:PRIVILEGE CREEP\nUsers accumulate roles\nacross job changes\nNever cleaned up;
    fork again
        #FF8800:MANUAL REVIEWS\n15-30 min per user per app\n200 users = 250+ person-hours\nper review cycle;
    end fork

    #CC3333:Audit findings + security incidents\n+ wasted time;
}

partition "WITH Integration (What Changes)" #EEFFEE {
    :Your app exports a daily\nuser/role file (CSV);
    note right
        **Your team's effort:**
        ONE-TIME: 2 hours setup
        ONGOING: automated daily
        (or 15 min/week if manual)
    end note

    :SailPoint automatically\ndetects who got new access;
    :Only CHANGED access\ngoes to managers for review;
    note right
        Day 1: 500 users - all reviewed (baseline)
        Day 2: identical - nothing happens
        Day 3: 1 new user - ONLY that
        manager gets a certification
    end note

    :Managers click\nApprove or Revoke;
    :Revocations tracked\nfor compliance evidence;

    fork
        #339933:AUDIT READY\nFull evidence trail\nSOX/SOC2 compliant\nReviews documented;
    fork again
        #339933:FAST DETECTION\nNew access reviewed\nwithin 24-48 hours\nnot 90+ days;
    fork again
        #339933:AUTO CLEANUP\nTerminated users\ndetected immediately\nwhen file is refreshed;
    fork again
        #339933:10x FASTER\nReviews take minutes\nnot hours\n(unified SailPoint dashboard);
    end fork

    #339933:Compliant + secure\n+ efficient;
}

partition "What YOU (Product Owner) Need to Do" #E8F4FD {
    :1. APPROVE the export format\n(review CSV template)\n~30 minutes;
    :2. ASSIGN someone to deliver\nthe file daily\n~15 minutes;
    :3. REVIEW your entitlement catalog\n(are role names/descriptions accurate?)\n~1-2 hours;
    :4. PARTICIPATE in first campaign\n(validate data quality)\n~30 minutes;

    note right
        **Total one-time effort: ~3 hours**
        **Ongoing: near zero** (automated)
        or 15 min/week (manual export)

        You are already responsible for
        knowing who has access. This just
        makes it **visible, reviewable,
        and auditable**.
    end note
}

stop

legend right
    **Key Compliance Frameworks:**
    SOX 404: Periodic access review required
    SOC 2 CC6.3: Access authorized + reviewed
    HIPAA 164.312: Access only to authorized persons
    PCI DSS 7/8: Need-to-know + review every 6 months
    NIST AC-2: Periodic account review + automated audit

    **Bottom Line:**
    Ungoverned apps are audit findings waiting to happen.
    A daily CSV file prevents this.
endlegend

@enduml
